Feature: The throttle stick in a hover
  In a hover mode, the throttle stick does not set the power. It sets how fast the plane
  climbs or descends. In the middle, the plane keeps its height. Push the stick above the
  middle and the plane climbs straight up. Pull it below the middle and the plane goes
  down.

  Expectation: A raised throttle stick lifts the plane
    Given the vehicle is armed
    And the autopilot mode is QLOITER
    And the plane is on the ground
    When the throttle stick is high
    Then the flight is hovering
    And the plane is flying
    And the height above home is at least 15 m

  Expectation: A centred throttle stick holds the height
    Given the flight is hovering
    And the plane is flying
    And the height above home is at least 5 m
    When the throttle stick is middle
    Then the flight is hovering
    And the height above home is at least 5 m

  Expectation: A lowered throttle stick brings the plane down
    Given the flight is hovering
    And the plane is flying
    And the height above home is at least 5 m
    When the throttle stick is low
    Then the plane is on the ground
